+    `WARNING`; the `rm()` warning names the leftover path so it can be removed by hand.
+  - **Signal-safe cleanup** — playwright's default `handleSIGINT` calls `process.exit()` itself,
+    which skips every `finally`, so before this was fixed each Ctrl-C leaked a 19–50MB throwaway
+    profile directory (holding a whole IDB) *and* an orphan Vite holding the `--strictPort` port,
+    making the next run on that port fail with an error that pointed nowhere near the cause
+    (reproduced 4/4). The collector now passes `handleSIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP: false`, registers the
+    live profile dirs / contexts / dev server, and runs the same idempotent teardown from its own
+    `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM`/`SIGHUP` handlers before exiting non-zero. This matters because the file
+    itself says the job takes "十几分钟" — Ctrl-C is the normal way a human aborts one.
+  - **Single process-tree root, single renderer** — the `ps` scan must find exactly one chromium
+    root for the run's unique `user-data-dir`, *and* exactly one renderer process. Ambiguity
+    throws rather than attributing RSS to the wrong tree, and since `rendererMaxRssMb` is defined
+    as "the largest renderer" while the protocol calls it the tab-OOM ground truth, a stray
+    spare/prerender renderer that happened to be larger would silently become the baseline number.
+  - **Sample integrity and dispersion** — samples that could not be read are excluded from the
+    medians *and* counted into `medians.sampleIntegrity`; every published metric additionally
+    carries `{ value, min, max, n, dropped }`. A single median hides whether a difference is even
+    above noise: `12×512`'s A-point delta has a cross-run spread larger than the median itself.
+    Metrics whose spread exceeds their own value are listed in
+    `sampleIntegrity.metricsWithSpreadOverValue` and warned about by name. All of these warnings
+    go to **stderr** (`console.warn`) so an stderr-only nightly wrapper cannot miss "1 of 3 runs
+    usable"; `--strict` turns dropped samples or a negative A-point delta into a non-zero exit.
+  - **Gate branch coverage** — `npm run bench:image-mem:gate-mutation` neutralizes each rejection
+    branch in `image-mem-gate.mjs` to `if (false)` and re-runs the contract tests; a branch whose
